.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:4:Record the Sparkle EdDSA update-signing key evidence and custody. The ed25519 keypair is generated and the PRIVATE key is placed into approved custody once inside Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta), alongside the Developer ID and notarization credentials. This task runs unattended afterwards and records the PUBLIC key, its fingerprint, the tool version, the generation date, and the custody location by name only, plus the rotation and revocation procedure. It deliberately stops there: pinning SUPublicEDKey, wiring the CI signing secret, and verifying a signed appcast are owned by TASK-260728-3bj9bk, because the generated macOS target, the updater integration, and the appcast pipeline do not exist yet. Completing this task does not mean self-update signing works.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:7:In scope: verifying that the keypair generated at Ceremony C1 exists and that the private key resides only in the approved custody store; recording the public key, its fingerprint, the pinned Sparkle vendor tool version, and the generation date as non-secret evidence; the rotation and revocation procedure for this keypair; a leak scan. Out of scope: generating the keypair or moving the private key (TASK-260728-q5kjta owns the ceremony); editing any Info.plist or project manifest; creating or binding CI secrets; signing or verifying an appcast; publishing release assets; any claim that the updater integration or CI signing path is complete.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:10:1. The keypair generated at Ceremony C1 is confirmed present and the pinned Sparkle vendor tool version and generation date are recorded. 2. The private key resides only in the approved custody store; it is absent from git, board resources, shell history, and logs, and its bytes are never echoed. 3. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records the public key value and fingerprint, the custody location by name only, and the rotation and revocation procedure. 4. The outcome states explicitly that SUPublicEDKey pinning and appcast signing verification remain open under TASK-260728-3bj9bk and are not evidenced here. 5. A post-run scan of the repository, board resources, and run logs finds no private key material.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/progress.md:14:- TASK-260728-q5kjta
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/progress.md:23:2026-07-28 replan (TASK-260728-3a2dnr): this task belongs to Ceremony C1, the single up-front human permission session on the current arm64 Mac. See the wave plan and ceremony script attached to TASK-260728-3a2dnr. Never request, echo, or persist secret values, key paths, or credential contents in board, repo, or logs.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/progress.md:24:2026-07-28 replan round 3 (TASK-260728-3a2dnr): now blocked by TASK-260728-q5kjta (Ceremony C1). Keypair generation and private-key custody moved into C1; this task records the public key, fingerprint, tool version, custody name, and rotation procedure. Name kept for cross-reference stability (ADR-026, TASK-260728-3bj9bk, .spec/platform-distribution.md, .spec/security-claims.md); downstream integration remains open.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-3jloqy_provision-app-ids-capabilities-and-development-profiles/README.md:4:Create exactly four macOS App IDs in the Relux Works Apple Developer account - works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel - enable the Network Extensions capability on all four, hosts included, and generate one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. Apple requires the packet-tunnel entitlement on the containing app as well as the embedded provider, so host App IDs are provisioned exactly like provider App IDs. No App Group record is created and the App Groups capability is enabled on nothing: rule G4 of the approved matrix (TASK-260715-ypo7yo) withholds com.apple.security.application-groups from every macOS target. There is no Keychain access-group portal mutation to perform at all, because keychain sharing has no portal record and rule K2 withholds keychain-access-groups from every macOS target. The human authorization for these mutations is granted once in Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta); this task is performed unattended by the agent using that granted session, and the human does not wait for it. Preserve reproducible non-secret metadata and validate each downloaded profile against the approved matrix. The four iOS identifiers stay defined in the matrix and are not provisioned on this path because iOS is deferred under ADR-024. If the portal forces a fresh two-factor challenge mid-run, record it as a named short re-authentication interaction rather than silently retrying.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:4:Prove and record the Keychain-only notarization custody required by ADR-025 before any notarization step is declared ready. The interactive notarytool store-credentials run and the owner disposition decision for the source App Store Connect API private-key file happen once inside Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta). This task runs unattended afterwards: it verifies that the NAMED Keychain profile authenticates against the real Apple notary service using only its name, records the non-secret evidence and the disposition the owner chose, defines rotation and revocation, and scans for leaks. The agent never receives, echoes, or persists secret values.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:7:In scope: a read-only notary history or whoami style authentication check performed with the named login-Keychain profile alone; recording the profile name, the fact a profile exists, the authenticating team identifier, and the check outcome; transcribing the owner-approved disposition chosen at C1 for the source .p8 file from Keychain-backed migration, retention under a named custodian with documented access control, or secure destruction, and verifying that the stated disposition actually holds; a repeatable rotation and revocation procedure keyed to the profile name; shell-history and command-echo suppression plus a post-run leak scan. Out of scope: performing the interactive store-credentials or making the disposition decision (TASK-260728-q5kjta owns both); recording or transmitting the source file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes anywhere; submitting a real notarization of a product artifact; configuring CI notarization secrets (TASK-260715-3gkwn0 owns the separately-scoped CI credential); Developer ID certificate issuance; iOS or App Store Connect distribution credentials.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:10:1. A read-only authentication check succeeds using only the named notarytool Keychain profile, with the command transcript showing no secret value. 2. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records the profile name, the authenticating team identifier, the check outcome, the date, and the rotation/revocation procedure; it records no file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 3. The owner-approved disposition of the source App Store Connect API private-key file chosen at Ceremony C1 is transcribed and independently verified to hold; a mode-0600 file left in place with no recorded custodian is an explicit fail. 4. Shell history and command echo are suppressed for every command, and a post-run scan of the repository, board resources, shell history, and run logs finds no notarization secret material. 5. If the profile is absent, fails to authenticate, or the disposition was not decided at C1, the task records the exact blocking input needed and remains blocked rather than reporting a ready notarization path.
