1782:- IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHDeferredSemanticReport` exposes `reported`, `notReported`, and `unsupported`. Exact receive-credit policy/snapshots, open reasons, exit metadata, KEX generation, window/server-rekey/keepalive metrics, and manual keepalive RTT now require one of those states; no default zero/false or mandatory full-fidelity policy remains. Host-before-auth, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client and server rekey handling, bounded buffers/backpressure, cancellation/lifecycle, Keychain-only credential references, keepalive transmission, available metrics, and privacy-safe errors remain mandatory.
